Subject: [PATCH] projectm-eval: read a lone '.' as the number 0, like NS-EEL

Local fix against projectM 4.1.7 plus patches 0001–0033. MilkDrop's NS-EEL
lexer accepts a lone '.' as a number and converts it with atof(), which gives 0,
so presets such as "zoom=zoom+.10*sin(rad+.+15.15)" or "y=if(c,.-.4,y)"
compile in MilkDrop. projectm-eval's FLOAT rule needs a digit and rejected the
character as an invalid token. Add a rule for a lone '.' before the catch-all.
Only code that failed before is affected. Scanner.c contains only the table and
action changes flex 2.6.4 generates for this rule (applied as the difference of
two runs of the same flex, so the committed generator skeleton is unchanged).
